From: Qianhui Xu <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] libcamera: simple: expose flash subdevices as camera
 controls

The simple pipeline handler only traverses the media graph from the
camera sensor to the video node, so flash (MEDIA_ENT_F_FLASH) and torch
entities are never opened and their V4L2 flash controls are unreachable
from applications: `cam` has no flash control to set, even when the
board describes its flash LED as a proper media entity (the Lenovo
Legion Y700 Gen 4 has one such LED, /dev/v4l-subdev*, driven by
leds-qcom-flash).

libcamera has no dedicated flash control ids yet, so expose the flash
subdevices' V4L2 controls directly:

- bind every MEDIA_ENT_F_FLASH entity to each camera (the media graph
  carries no flash-to-sensor association; boards with a flash have one
  rear camera), keeping the already-opened V4L2Subdevice;
- merge the subdevices' V4L2 control info into the camera's control set
  in init(), with a merged control id map (the ControlId instances are
  owned by the flash subdevices, which live as long as the pipeline
  handler);
- in queueRequestDevice(), apply request controls that belong to a flash
  subdevice directly to it; they are not passed to the IPA (which only
  looks up the controls it knows).

Applications (cam --list-controls, cam --controls=...) can now set
V4L2_CID_FLASH_LED_MODE / _STROBE / _TORCH_INTENSITY etc. like any other
camera control.  A real libcamera flash API (controls::Flash + IPA
integration) remains future work; this is the minimal path to make the
App-usable torch/strobe reachable from libcamera.

Signed-off-by: Qianhui Xu <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
